WEBVTT

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.290
So, how about right now?

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.470
Oi, don't go sleeping down--

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.530
Once again, the victim was a prostitute.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:01:00.330
This is now the second murder
to take place in Whitechapel.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.250
"Jack the Ripper"...

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.980
<i>Tripped up by your twisted words</i>

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.740
<i>I can't fall asleep at night</i>

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.870
<i>Transfixed by your gaze</i>

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.910
<i>I feel your sickness inside</i>

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:44.330
<i>Injured, I break down</i>

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:47.710
<i>this never-ending punishment</i>

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:52.090
<i>I feel your sins all the time</i>

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:56.680
<i>It's inescapable, take me away</i>

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:00.270
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:04.390
<i>Show me a dream that will stir me awake</i>

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:08.020
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.150
<i>Whenever I awaken, you fall apart</i>

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.240
<i>Someday... (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.580
<i>Find me (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.040
<i>Steal your heart (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.920
<i>Endlessly (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.710
<i>I will scream aloud</i>

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:42.890
The Phantom of Whitechapel Act 1

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.690
Please use this room, Mr Bonde.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.360
Wah! You idiot! What are you
opening the door for?!

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.820
You're a woman! Stay out of here!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.830
As of today, I'm going to be using
this room, too. Cheers.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:05.460
Huh?! Louis, do something about this!

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.920
Mr Bonde is a man now,
so I do not see any problem.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:09.880
Imbecile!

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:15.050
Moran, I am a man.
I'd like you to treat me as a man.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:19.050
This is me asking it for myself,
so you need not pay me any mind.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.760
You may be fine with it,
but I don't accept it!

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.560
Besides, there are <i>other</i>
issues as well, right?

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:25.980
Issues?

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.940
It is all right. I am quite confident
that I can pass as a man.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.230
I don't just mean appearances.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:36.150
You're no match for a man when it
comes to upper body strength.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.320
If we're on a mission, and--

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:46.080
You don't quit. If you're this dead-set
on not recognising me as a man...

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.250
...shall we put it to the test, Moran?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.800
Wh-What does that mean?!
That's terrifying! Put <i>what </i>to the test?!

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.630
I heard a fuss going on up here.
What is the matter?

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:02.390
William! Listen to this! She said--

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:07.350
I was saying that I would like
to use this room, as well.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.520
What do you think about that, Will?

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.400
Are you saying that you're taking
some issue with a fellow man...

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.900
...sharing the same room?

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.320
W-William, you little...

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.910
Honestly! You've got William
twisted around your finger...

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.750
Moran, what will it take
for you to acknowledge me?

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:36.340
It's not a question of acknowledging;
it's a question of how useful you are.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:40.630
Is everyone here?

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:44.390
I would like all of you to work
on something together today.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:47.600
Together? You mean, her too?!

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.230
Of course.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.350
As the senior operative,
you have to offer your support.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:56.280
Albert has asked you to take
charge of Bonde, right?

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:59.190
Yeah, he did say that, but...

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.910
The details of the job
are written in here.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:07.160
I need to... take a little
rest right now...

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:13.210
Brother, you will catch
a cold if you sleep there.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.250
Will is having a nap?

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.510
It's like a reaction he has
after overexerting his mind.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:22.550
When William gets like this,
he doesn't wake up for anything.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:26.010
Now, as for the details of our mission...

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.730
A key?

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:36.570
Ooh, look at those people!

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:39.150
Wow! How handsome.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.740
Smashing!

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.700
So handsome!

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:51.250
Hmph, I get it--Bonde leaves
no room for doubt as a man.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.580
Be that as it may,

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.880
going to fetch the contents of
a safe deposit box at the bank...

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.960
...is a child's errand,
one that doesn't need me--

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.920
No.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:04.380
Brother William ordered
<i>all </i>of us to do this.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.100
Louis, don't be so by-the-book.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.850
Fred, is there something on your mind?

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:19.270
William made it a point that all
of us were assigned to this mission.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.860
It's out of the ordinary.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.030
That's the feeling I get.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:27.280
I see. Still,
regardless of what it entails,

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:31.580
we merely need to carry out the
assignment given to us, don't we?

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:34.920
The assignment given to us, eh?

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:43.300
Yes, it's true! I was off duty,
but then Smith suddenly took ill!

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:47.050
Is that right? Things have been rough
around here lately, so I'm grateful.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:50.350
Just leave it to me!
I will arrest any criminal,

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:53.140
no matter how heinous they may be!

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.770
I would like to access
my safe deposit box.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:02.900
Well, well, Mr Moriarty. I will go
get things ready at once.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.490
Please wait for me in the parlour.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:16.250
This is taking too long.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.500
Wh-Who are you people?!

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:23.420
Keep calm! And don't try anything funny!

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:27.800
Keys! Hand over your keys!

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.760
Get your hands up, and go stand in
the corner of the room! Do it now!

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:41.730
You two take the vault.
You take the safe deposit boxes.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:44.110
Load up anything that looks valuable.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:47.070
Bollocks, that must be the leader.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:51.490
I wasn't expecting my chance
at promotion to come so soon--

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.080
Lie down and stay quiet, Yard rat!

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.000
On your feet! You and you are going
to blindfold the customers.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.790
Look lively!

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:02.800
A bank robbery. Now, of all times?

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:06.510
We can't allow the package that
William asked us for to be taken.

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:09.430
But the hostages are a concern, as well.

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:14.600
If I carry out my role well here, the
others will accept me as one of them...

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:18.270
Where did they go?

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:22.020
Does this mean that Will's mission
takes priority over the hostages?

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.980
I'm already getting a late start!

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:38.330
You are skilful indeed.
Where are the other two?

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.830
What are you talking about, Bonde?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.840
I'm only here because I was
the one with the key.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:44.630
Huh?

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:50.010
The other two are each doing their
own jobs. It's not like they're kids.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:53.510
When did you split up the jobs to do?

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:57.140
Ah, so that's how it is, all right.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:01.230
You said something about merely doing
the assignments given to us,

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:03.440
which gave me pause.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:07.440
It turns out you're someone who
takes no initiative, aren't you?

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:12.030
T-Takes no initiative? You mean,
I'm supposed to be off on my own?

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:15.830
Going off on your own and deciding
for yourself what needs to be done

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:17.410
are two different things.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:24.000
This is hopeless. I guess I'll have to
start teaching you from the top.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:28.300
First, what is it we need
to do in this situation?

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:33.720
We absolutely cannot allow the item
from the safe deposit box,

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:35.800
the objective of our mission, to be taken.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.260
Correct.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.390
And now that our mission is accomplished,

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:43.900
we <i>could </i>leave the scene.
So what do we do?

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.150
We can't.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:46.980
If we leave here the way things are,

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.400
then once they wake up,
they might kill the hostages.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:54.200
So what do we do about them? Kill them?

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:57.700
We can't do that, either.
If we aggravate the situation,

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.910
then the Yard's investigation
will become overblown,

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.920
and there's a risk that Holmes
might get involved.

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:06.460
We don't want the fact that one of the
Moriarty family was here to be known,

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.340
even if it was only by coincidence.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:14.090
We need to bring an end to this in a way
that keeps Holmes from taking notice.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:17.050
So what should we do, then?

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.690
Beat the robbers in such a way
that no one knows it was us,

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:27.150
and rescue the hostages.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:31.360
Right. That's the important part.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:33.360
You can consider for yourself
what you'd like to do,

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.450
so long as it doesn't deviate
from what needs to be done.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:39.160
What I'd like...?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:43.210
The vault room is secure.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:45.460
There are four hostiles in the main hall.

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:48.210
It's a large room
and they are spread out,

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:51.260
so it will be difficult to take them
down without anyone noticing.

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:53.130
That's a problem, all right.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.970
How exciting.

00:10:55.970 --> 00:11:00.310
If I can do as I'd like to,
then that's just what I'll do.

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:02.430
I never was one...

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:07.150
...to fit into any one mould.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:13.650
I have an idea to get out of this.
Will you work with me?

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:27.170
Grr, what is taking them so long?

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:29.710
Oi, somebody go see what's--

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:33.090
What's happening?!

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:34.470
The lights...!

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.760
One!

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.220
Two!

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:43.720
Three!

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.180
Four!

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.600
Five!

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.020
Six!

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.440
Seven!

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.610
Eight!

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.820
Wake up! Please, wake up!

00:11:58.820 --> 00:11:59.870
Huh?!

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:02.740
Wow, you were truly amazing!

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:06.580
Leave it to one of London's
vaunted officers of the Yard.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.670
I-I did <i>that</i>?!

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.210
I don't remember any of it.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:16.220
You were so excited, it's only natural
that you wouldn't remember.

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:19.470
Geoff, that was quite the feat!

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:28.350
That was mere child's play!

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:33.980
Didn't I tell you? I can arrest
any villain who crosses me!

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:38.740
That was quite the ingenious plan, Bonde.

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:42.530
Imagine, using the muzzle flashes
in all that darkness.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:49.710
I couldn't have done it on my own.
It's all thanks to you, Moran.

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:54.670
Taking out all four of them in the main
hall in one shot without killing them...

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:58.800
...and then pinning the feat
on that buffoon of a cop,

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:01.430
both earned you more than passing marks.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:06.470
I look forward to next time, Bonde.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:09.100
Let's toast our first successful
mission together.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.060
Only one swig, though.

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:22.160
Louis... I recognised
who those robbers were.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:25.200
Do you think this incident might have...?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:30.250
Were they employed in order
to bring us closer to Mr Bonde?

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:33.750
H-Hey!

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:33.750
Indeed.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:37.840
I would not be surprised
if Brother set this up.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:43.430
Bonde! There's hardly any left!

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.890
You've wasted no time
in disrespecting your senior!

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:51.390
Ho, now look who's
talking like that, Moran.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.980
Gah! Old man!

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:56.230
Er, I mean, M-Master...

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.820
Master?

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:02.950
This brings back memories.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:06.120
Who is this gentleman?

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:12.210
The old man's name is Jack Renfield.

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:14.330
During the First Anglo-Afghan War,

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:19.420
he was feared as Britain's master
close-quarters combatant.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.630
He was known as...

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.930
..."Jack the Ripper."

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:39.480
This old man is the one true
"Jack the Ripper."

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:44.070
One true...? Then, you mean that
other serial killer is a fake?

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:51.540
Must be. It was over half a century ago
when the old man went by that name.

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:53.910
Isn't that right, Master?

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:59.290
I suppose they did call me that
dreadful name once upon a time.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.710
Seriously, <i>this </i>is when you play
at being an old man?

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:06.640
I'm sure that a serial killer who assumed
your nickname has turned up,

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:08.680
and that's why William has called you in.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:09.930
Moran...

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:12.930
That isn't why.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:16.150
Are you all right?
You should get more rest.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:19.650
No, I need to inform
you all of some details.

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:25.360
It has been too long, Master William.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:30.530
Please request whatever you wish
of this old man in his waning years.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:33.450
I would be more than grateful.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:40.040
You needn't be so formal. Feel free to
call me "Young Will," as usual. Besides...

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:45.220
...you brushed my cheek earlier whilst
I was still sleeping, didn't you, Maestro?

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:50.640
You knew about that?!
Same old Young Will as ever!

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:54.350
So, why exactly <i>did</i>
you call the old man in?

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:55.680
Right.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:59.690
As you all know,
the serial killer in Whitechapel

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:03.070
has been using the maestro's old nickname
to claim credit for the killings.

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:05.440
Which is why...

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:08.820
...he said that he would like to
assist in disposing of the killer

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:11.490
who has adopted his name...

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:16.710
...and approached me in my capacity
as crime consultant. Thus,

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:22.590
I had all of you go and retrieve the
maestro's tools of the trade in advance.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:25.090
I trust there were no problems with that?

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:29.890
No, it was no problem at all.

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:31.390
Right, Bonde?

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:33.260
Of course not.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:39.060
I'm curious, when you call him "Maestro,"

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.860
what sort of relationship do you
have with each other?

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:45.480
Ah, we haven't yet told you
that part, have we?

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:47.360
Following the fire,

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:52.700
we stayed in the home of Lord Rockwell,
who was our guardian for a time.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:57.160
The butler of the estate there...

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:59.330
...was Maestro Jack.

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:02.750
Come in.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:10.970
Well, well, the lads from
the House of Moriarty...

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:13.640
Is there something I can do for you?

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:18.020
Jack Renfield, we have an earnest
request to make of you.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:20.140
Oh? What might that be?

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:24.770
I know through my observations
that you are former British military,

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.530
a crackerjack soldier who
served in Afghanistan.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:33.320
How does he know that? And what does
he mean, "through observation"?

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:37.750
Additionally, my research shows that you
earned the nickname "Jack the Ripper,"

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:41.960
and that you were feared
by both friend and foe alike.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:49.340
I have only told the lord of the
estate about my past life.

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:56.100
So, what sort of request would you like
to make of this feeble old man?

00:17:56.100 --> 00:18:00.100
For us to be able to survive
on our own hereafter,

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:03.230
we would like for you to teach us
how to protect ourselves.

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:06.150
For you to be able to survive on your own?

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:20.200
Very well! I will teach you what you
will need to protect yourselves--

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.920
or rather, more accurately speaking...

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:27.130
...how to kill a man.

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:33.880
The maestro taught us all sorts of things.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:37.220
It is because of the maestro
that we are who we are at all,

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:39.180
Moran and Fred included.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.390
Is that right?

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:44.390
Once we find out who the real killer is,

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:48.900
it will become clear whether they have
anything to do with the maestro.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:52.900
We will purge society of this phoney
Jack the Ripper, who is causing a scandal,

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:57.370
and remove the disgrace from the
maestro's name. Besides which,

00:18:57.370 --> 00:19:03.000
we cannot overlook the fact that those
who are weak are being preyed upon.

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:19.850
Whitechapel. Things never
change here, either.

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:21.470
What was that?

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:22.720
--Sod off!
--Get out!

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:25.060
Get on out of here, you bloody Yard rats!

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:27.730
We'll keep this town safe ourselves!

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:31.690
Yeah! We're gonna kill
that serial murderer!

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:35.200
Why are the locals facing off
against the Yard?

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:38.320
They're both after the same
criminal, aren't they?

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:42.700
Let us deal with arresting the killer!
We're here to protect the citizenry!

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:47.170
How can you say that now?!
You haven't investigated anything so far!

00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:50.880
You don't even think of us
as "citizenry" anyhow!

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:57.340
The townsfolk are fit to be tied.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:02.470
Yeah. One false step and this
dramatic killer has what it takes

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:06.390
to transform the people--
in fact, the whole town.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:10.020
This town is now a battlefield.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:15.570
Those bloody pests!

00:20:15.570 --> 00:20:18.780
As of this moment, I'm declaring
that Scotland Yard's top priority

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:21.450
is to disarm that Vigilance Committee!

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:23.410
Chief Inspector Arterton!

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:27.120
Our priority should really be
the safety of the citizens!

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:31.420
I believe we should continue to focus
our efforts on arresting this criminal!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:36.220
Lestrade, you don't understand
the nature of things here, do you?

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:39.680
It makes no difference to us how
many of those poors get killed

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:41.550
by that murdering maniac!

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:46.430
But if those vigilantes stage an uprising,
it will all be too late!

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:51.940
Remember Bloody Sunday,
when the paupers clashed with us!

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:55.940
We can never have a repeat
of that mistake.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.740
Who cares how many whores get killed?!

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:01.620
Give disarming the Vigilance
Committee your priority!

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:02.950
Sir!

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:12.250
My word, Chief Inspector Arterton
is in a foul humour.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.670
The commissioner--

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:18.510
no, even the interior minister must be
putting a lot of pressure on him.

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:21.760
Paterson, I'm stepping away
for an hour or so.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:24.930
Will you handle it if any
emergencies come up?

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:29.020
Of course, Lestrade.
We're chums, aren't we?

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:37.320
I see.

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:39.450
What are you reading?

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:42.490
Investigative reports from
our man inside the Yard.

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:44.160
An inside man?

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:48.080
You and he will likely be working
together before long.

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:50.460
Oh? I can't wait.

00:21:50.460 --> 00:21:55.210
It looks as though the Yard is nowhere
near closing in on the killer.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:22:00.840
Yes. They seem fixated on this case as
the work of a single psychotic killer,

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:04.800
but I am clearly able to see
the full scope of these killings.

00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:10.140
We're going to show these
phoney Jack the Rippers...

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:14.860
...who the real devils
around this town are.

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:23.610
<i>Fate that over time changes</i>
<i>into chains of sorrow,</i>

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:31.830
<i>leave me the light of rebirth</i>
<i>for the world ahead</i>

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:42.420
<i>Struck by a frustration</i>
<i>I'd never experienced before,</i>

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:45.800
<i>I feel lost, I feel lost</i>

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:49.810
<i>The letters I dashed off</i>
<i>are all I remember</i>

00:22:49.810 --> 00:22:53.190
<i>It's all true, it's all true</i>

00:22:53.190 --> 00:23:00.610
<i>Witness as I forgo my forsaken future</i>
<i>with no regrets</i>

00:23:00.610 --> 00:23:09.200
<i>and you will win your intent</i>
<i>at the expense of becoming my pawn</i>

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:17.000
<i>A scarlet thread fluttering in the wind</i>
<i>at five in the morning</i>

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:23.260
<i>I'll recover my memories on the last day</i>

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:26.050
<i>Hold me down till the end</i>

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:31.720
<i>Finish by wiping away my sins,</i>

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:38.400
<i>warning me to stay true if I desire beauty</i>

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:52.030
The Phantom of Whitechapel

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:52.030
Act 2

00:23:46.740 --> 00:23:52.240
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Phantom of Whitechapel Act 2."
